{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CfwibSwku5YotNpDSYze9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I haven't opened the dashboard or waited for the rule to run, so neither has been checked beyond the create calls succeeding. The rule's status was still \"pending\" when it was created.\n\n**Data:** The data view `Kibana Sample Data Logs` has a `timestamp` field and these fields I used or noted:\n- `response`, a string field with a `.keyword` subfield\n- `bytes`\n- `extension`\n- `clientip`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `machine.os`\n- `host`\n- `url`\n- `agent`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-97ef19ec Web logs overview\" has four panels. You can open it at `http://localhost:15601/app/dashboards#/view/eff-97ef19ec-web-logs-overview-9bc763c1b589`.\n- Total requests, as a single number\n- Requests over time, as a line chart\n- Requests by response code, as a pie chart\n- Average bytes by file extension, as a bar chart\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-97ef19ec 5xx spike\" (id `0e43a2bb-d833-4cf5-b7a5-5c15389ae15c`) runs every minute. It counts documents in `kibana_sample_data_logs` whose `response.keyword` matches `5[0-9][0-9]` over a 5-minute window. It fires when that count is above 10. It has no actions attached, so it will only show up as an alert in Kibana and won't send any notification.\n\nThe sample data's timestamps may not be recent, so the rule may not fire even if the data contains 5xx responses."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1188,"cache_read_input_tokens":19897,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1188},"output_tokens":541,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a4eb1cb7-866c-5bbf